From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Stuerz <simon.stuerz@nymea.io>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Use Boost.Process v1 API explicitly for Boost 1.86+

Upstream-Status: Pending

systemImpl.cpp uses the classic Boost.Process API (boost::process::
ipstream, child, args, std_out unqualified). Boost 1.86+ restructured
Boost.Process into v1/v2, with boost::process defaulting to the new v2
API and <boost/process.hpp> no longer pulling in the v1 headers at all
(ipstream/child/args live under boost/process/v1/*.hpp, and v1 is only
an inline namespace -- making its names resolve unqualified -- when
BOOST_PROCESS_VERSION is explicitly defined as 1 before inclusion).

Define BOOST_PROCESS_VERSION 1 and include <boost/process/v1.hpp>
directly instead of the version-agnostic <boost/process.hpp>, so the
existing unqualified v1 API usage below keeps compiling unchanged.

Found while building against Boost 1.90.0 under the wrynose Yocto BSP
port.

Signed-off-by: Simon Stuerz <simon.stuerz@nymea.io>
---
 modules/SystemAggregator/system/systemImpl.cpp | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/modules/SystemAggregator/system/systemImpl.cpp
+++ b/modules/SystemAggregator/system/systemImpl.cpp
@@ -13,7 +13,14 @@
 #include <thread>
 #include <vector>
 #include <fmt/chrono.h>
-#include <boost/process.hpp>
+// BOOST_PROCESS_VERSION 1: this file uses the classic Boost.Process
+// API (ipstream, child, args, std_out), which Boost 1.86+ moved under
+// an explicit boost::process::v1 namespace (boost::process now
+// defaults to the v2 API, and <boost/process.hpp> no longer pulls in
+// the v1 headers at all). Defining this makes v1 an inline namespace
+// again, so the unqualified names below keep resolving.
+#define BOOST_PROCESS_VERSION 1
+#include <boost/process/v1.hpp>
 #include "../systemaggregator_upload_log_request.hpp"
 
 using namespace std::chrono_literals;
